(2962242, 410693, 36060, '<td valign="top">Wonderful image, congrats on your first ribbon!</td>', 'Wonderful image, congrats on your first ribbon!', '2006-10-25 17:00:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2962258, 410693, 714, '<td valign="top">Wow, way sweet shot!  Love the glow and color.  Beautiful!</td>', 'Wow, way sweet shot!  Love the glow and color.  Beautiful!', '2006-10-25 17:04:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2962313, 411730, 42013, '<td valign="top">Interesting shot i found while browsing. I like the light in the frame and think that a stronger composition could have been achieved by moving subject to the right, leaving the brightest part of the picture more off centered. This would have also given more separation between light source and subject. You know your stuff so not trying to criticize, JMHO.</td>', 'Interesting shot i found while browsing. I like the light in the frame and think that a stronger composition could have been achieved by moving subject to the right, leaving the brightest part of the picture more off centered. This would have also given more separation between light source and subject. You know your stuff so not trying to criticize, JMHO.', '2006-10-25 17:21:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2962488, 413108, 41554, '<td valign="top">Congratulations...<br/> <br/>Parabéns!! E obrigado pelo "light setup"!!</td>', 'Congratulations... Parabéns!! E obrigado pelo "light setup"!!', '2006-10-25 18:10:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2962561, 410673, 23203, '<td valign="top">Wow, you were robbed - look at all these 1/2/3 votes... if I were SC, I''d investigate those.<br/></td>', 'Wow, you were robbed - look at all these 1/2/3 votes... if I were SC, I''d investigate those.', '2006-10-25 18:31:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2962573, 410673, 37961, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote on this one, but clearly we have some non sci-fi lovers out there that just can''t appreciate the impact of this shot. I love it.  <br/> <br/>After challenge 10.</td>', 'I didn''t vote on this one, but clearly we have some non sci-fi lovers out there that just can''t appreciate the impact of this shot. I love it.   After challenge 10.', '2006-10-25 18:35:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2962581, 412399, 37961, '<td valign="top">Way underrated. This could be a movie cover. Hauntingly beautiful.</td>', 'Way underrated. This could be a movie cover. Hauntingly beautiful.', '2006-10-25 18:37:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2962605, 412929, 32997, '<td valign="top">I predict a shot that I love...</td>', 'I predict a shot that I love...', '2006-10-25 18:43:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2962628, 412984, 64489, '<td valign="top">Who gives this kind of photograph a 5 or a 6?<br/> <br/>Good job, Siggav - your ribbon is well-deserved.</td>', 'Who gives this kind of photograph a 5 or a 6? Good job, Siggav - your ribbon is well-deserved.', '2006-10-25 18:49:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2962654, 412929, 14620, '<td valign="top">Hmmmm ... just a wee bit off, weren''t you? ;-)  <br/> <br/>Kick ass shot Lesley!</td>', 'Hmmmm ... just a wee bit off, weren''t you? ;-)   Kick ass shot Lesley!', '2006-10-25 18:54:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2962718, 412336, 7810, '<td valign="top">Not a bad outing for your first challenge. i like the effect with the negative space. Nice work here keep at it!</td>', 'Not a bad outing for your first challenge. i like the effect with the negative space. Nice work here keep at it!', '2006-10-25 19:05:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2962767, 412654, 46870, '<td valign="top">Great shot ... Congradulations!<br/>Love it...........</td>', 'Great shot ... Congradulations!Love it...........', '2006-10-25 19:16:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(2962802, 412654, 56417, '<td valign="top">this is simply incredible!</td>', 'this is simply incredible!', '2006-10-25 19:25:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(2962890, 413302, 45475, '<td valign="top">I think the single beam makes the statement well. But I can understand your frustration. I''ll echo both photojournaliste and posthumous comments as well, I think they sum it up nicely :) Great stuff.</td>', 'I think the single beam makes the statement well. But I can understand your frustration. I''ll echo both photojournaliste and posthumous comments as well, I think they sum it up nicely :) Great stuff.', '2006-10-25 19:45:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(2962941, 412595, 42013, '<td valign="top">Here is my stab at the pic... First, it seems rather heavy on the RH side of the frame with the heavy shadow area. The light behind the cat provides such a bright spot that it overshadows the image of the cat and its silhoette(sp). I think the picture would have benefited by a little less shadow on the RH and placement of the light behind the cat or even out of the frame. <br/> <br/>OK, i reallize most cats don''t pose on command so it would be hard to make this happen but i think the picture(and the score) might have been improved.<br/> <br/>Picture also seems a bit soft, maybe the .8s shutter speed was responsible for this. Overal, not an unpleasing photo, just one that needs some compositional and technical tweaks to really make it shine. And never underestimate some people''s hatred of cats! :)</td>', 'Here is my stab at the pic... First, it seems rather heavy on the RH side of the frame with the heavy shadow area. The light behind the cat provides such a bright spot that it overshadows the image of the cat and its silhoette(sp). I think the picture would have benefited by a little less shadow on the RH and placement of the light behind the cat or even out of the frame.  OK, i reallize most cats don''t pose on command so it would be hard to make this happen but i think the picture(and the score) might have been improved. Picture also seems a bit soft, maybe the .8s shutter speed was responsible for this. Overal, not an unpleasing photo, just one that needs some compositional and technical tweaks to really make it shine. And never underestimate some people''s hatred of cats! :)', '2006-10-25 19:54:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2962948, 412595, 57620, '<td valign="top">The subject for me was the cat the light didn''t highlight the cat in anyway in fact the cat is underexposed. also the dark shadow on the right is distracting and could have been cropped out. The kitchen in the background also doesn''t ad to the shot. <br/> <br/>I would suggest getting lower and closer eliminate the distractions and more light on the subject.</td>', 'The subject for me was the cat the light didn''t highlight the cat in anyway in fact the cat is underexposed. also the dark shadow on the right is distracting and could have been cropped out. The kitchen in the background also doesn''t ad to the shot.  I would suggest getting lower and closer eliminate the distractions and more light on the subject.', '2006-10-25 19:55:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2962979, 412595, 14614, '<td valign="top">I would agree with the "heavy" comment on the right as well as the kitchen pulling my eye (and not being an important element in the composition).  WHile the back door frame appears to be straight, the formost wall isn''t (adding a bit of distraction).  The cat''s pose didn''t engagement (no face, tough to see) and light didn''t help send a message other than "night"  Those factors kept it in the middle of the pack for me.</td>', 'I would agree with the "heavy" comment on the right as well as the kitchen pulling my eye (and not being an important element in the composition).  WHile the back door frame appears to be straight, the formost wall isn''t (adding a bit of distraction).  The cat''s pose didn''t engagement (no face, tough to see) and light didn''t help send a message other than "night"  Those factors kept it in the middle of the pack for me.', '2006-10-25 20:01:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2963099, 412654, 40667, '<td valign="top">amazing. I''ve got an uncle up in Yellowknife who was telling me how amazing the lights are this year, thanks for showing us a little part</td>', 'amazing. I''ve got an uncle up in Yellowknife who was telling me how amazing the lights are this year, thanks for showing us a little part', '2006-10-25 20:26:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2963100, 412654, 66267, '<td valign="top">Yeah, I knew this would score well ;-)</td>', 'Yeah, I knew this would score well ;-)', '2006-10-25 20:27:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2963118, 411295, 66267, '<td valign="top">This should have gotten a ribbon.<br/> <br/>See, this is why DPC is not the best way to judge your pictures. I go by the comments people give, and not by the score you get, because people who post comments are distinguished from those obnoxious few who like tampering with the voting system (yes, you know who you are!). People who post comments that sound proffesional usually know what they''re talking about.<br/> <br/>And btw, almost everyone who posted a comment here gave this pic a very score.</td>', 'This should have gotten a ribbon. See, this is why DPC is not the best way to judge your pictures. I go by the comments people give, and not by the score you get, because people who post comments are distinguished from those obnoxious few who like tampering with the voting system (yes, you know who you are!). People who post comments that sound proffesional usually know what they''re talking about. And btw, almost everyone who posted a comment here gave this pic a very score.', '2006-10-25 20:30:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2963144, 410693, 66267, '<td valign="top">[quote] (would have loved to burn the buildings in the back, really makes the shot stand out more .. but alas basic editing applies!) <br/>[/quote]<br/> <br/>No no no! It''s because the buildings and the boats share the same values and colours the picture is interersting. The buildings go very well with the boats.</td>', '[quote] (would have loved to burn the buildings in the back, really makes the shot stand out more .. but alas basic editing applies!) [/quote] No no no! It''s because the buildings and the boats share the same values and colours the picture is interersting. The buildings go very well with the boats.', '2006-10-25 20:36:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2963238, 411730, 57882, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mpeters:</b></div><hr/><i> Interesting shot i found while browsing. I like the light in the frame and think that a stronger composition could have been achieved by moving subject to the right, leaving the brightest part of the picture more off centered. This would have also given more separation between light source and subject. You know your stuff so not trying to criticize, JMHO. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I welcome all comments, and yours makes perfect sense.  Thanks for the feedback.</td>', 'Originally posted by mpeters: Interesting shot i found while browsing. I like the light in the frame and think that a stronger composition could have been achieved by moving subject to the right, leaving the brightest part of the picture more off centered. This would have also given more separation between light source and subject. You know your stuff so not trying to criticize, JMHO.   I welcome all comments, and yours makes perfect sense.  Thanks for the feedback.', '2006-10-25 20:58:42.000000', NULL, 0),
