(3021289, 413314, 50695, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 6. I felt it didn''t quite come together to create a brilliant photograph, but I admired the experiment.</td>', 'I gave this a 6. I felt it didn''t quite come together to create a brilliant photograph, but I admired the experiment.', '2006-11-10 23:44:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(3021890, 412265, 43031, '<td valign="top">Frankly, Skip, and I''m speaking as a fan here, This is not your most amazing work. I think you got lost in how hard it was to light, while forgetting to project the presence and spirit of the situation with your lighting. <br/> <br/>I think if you''d gotten the flash off camera to the right and cross-lit the subjects this would have been better. I know I''m not the pro, but I know that I have seen you do better. <br/> <br/>You do know how to score well at DPC, whether you want to anymore or not. I''ve been blessed to be able to view your work here over the past year, and I''d hate for you to stop now because of this.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-11-11 13:53:51.</i></td>', 'Frankly, Skip, and I''m speaking as a fan here, This is not your most amazing work. I think you got lost in how hard it was to light, while forgetting to project the presence and spirit of the situation with your lighting.  I think if you''d gotten the flash off camera to the right and cross-lit the subjects this would have been better. I know I''m not the pro, but I know that I have seen you do better.  You do know how to score well at DPC, whether you want to anymore or not. I''ve been blessed to be able to view your work here over the past year, and I''d hate for you to stop now because of this.', '2006-11-11 13:20:53.000000', '2006-11-11 13:53:51.000000', 0),
(3025000, 412807, 60862, '<td valign="top">Well, you had me laughing!</td>', 'Well, you had me laughing!', '2006-11-13 00:29:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3025300, 412807, 28742, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pixeldust:</b></div><hr/><i> I don''t get what your purpose is here. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>LOL! That one''s going in my profile!</td>', 'Originally posted by pixeldust: I don''t get what your purpose is here.  LOL! That one''s going in my profile!', '2006-11-13 01:49:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(3039950, 413074, 5792, '<td valign="top">This is my favorite image of yours so far. The orientation of the sunset with the tree on the right, which itself helps frame the extended pier below, gives the composition wonderful balance. The sky color and clouds are stunning.<br/> <br/>The tree is a bit oversharpened, you can see a small amount of white haloing in the branches. I''d recommend correcting that for show. Could be my monitor is dark, but it looks like the pier on the right side in particular is a bit lost in the shadows. You might consider dodging the pier to bring out more light from behind it to add better definition to the pier itself.<br/> <br/>This is great image worthy of a gallery showing. I''d be proud to have it in my sunrise/sunset collections.</td>', 'This is my favorite image of yours so far. The orientation of the sunset with the tree on the right, which itself helps frame the extended pier below, gives the composition wonderful balance. The sky color and clouds are stunning. The tree is a bit oversharpened, you can see a small amount of white haloing in the branches. I''d recommend correcting that for show. Could be my monitor is dark, but it looks like the pier on the right side in particular is a bit lost in the shadows. You might consider dodging the pier to bring out more light from behind it to add better definition to the pier itself. This is great image worthy of a gallery showing. I''d be proud to have it in my sunrise/sunset collections.', '2006-11-17 10:42:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3042864, 412984, 31637, '<td valign="top">amazing contrast.</td>', 'amazing contrast.', '2006-11-18 23:35:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3043149, 412406, 64209, '<td valign="top">Am just revisiting.  I suspect you got ''average'' votes in the main because the image lacks impact, IMHO.  The sky, which was your reason for the shoot in the first place, was so dramatic it deserved more of the frame, and I would have personally been tempted to crop more of the ground off and possibly the area to the left of the needle.  A bit of USM and possibly a bit of play with the colours would have given you the WOW you needed for this shot.<br/> <br/>Having said all that, when I voted, I gave it a 7.  Why didn''t I comment at the time?  Dunno.</td>', 'Am just revisiting.  I suspect you got ''average'' votes in the main because the image lacks impact, IMHO.  The sky, which was your reason for the shoot in the first place, was so dramatic it deserved more of the frame, and I would have personally been tempted to crop more of the ground off and possibly the area to the left of the needle.  A bit of USM and possibly a bit of play with the colours would have given you the WOW you needed for this shot. Having said all that, when I voted, I gave it a 7.  Why didn''t I comment at the time?  Dunno.', '2006-11-19 05:46:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(3043266, 412039, 60915, '<td valign="top">Beautiful tones and lighting, love the nostalgic feel. Absolutely wonderful image.</td>', 'Beautiful tones and lighting, love the nostalgic feel. Absolutely wonderful image.', '2006-11-19 07:21:57.000000', NULL, 0),
